    "metadata": {
      "title": "HISTOR snapshot 2026-10-20: MCP tool definitions and how they change",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23512760",
      "publication_date": "2026-10-20",
      "description": "<p>HISTOR reads the tool list (`tools/list`) of every remote MCP server in the official MCP registry<br>once a day, and of npm/PyPI MCP packages run in a sandbox once per published version (new versions<br>first, a few hundred a day). It records the exact tool definitions,<br>pins them by digest, and writes a signed label to a public RFC 9162 Merkle log whenever a tool set<br>first appears, stays the same, or changes. This snapshot is that record as files.</p>\n<p>- **81,879** listed servers (31,040 remote endpoints, 50,839 packages), plus 2,078 delisted<br>- **38,126** with a recorded tool set; **9,340** changed at least once<br>- **23,821** recorded changes, 2026-09-24 to 2026-10-20<br>- **57,846** distinct tool sets (current ones and every one a change replaced)<br>- **636** servers with a block-tier WARDEN pattern match, **14,379** advise-only</p>\n<p>Live view and per-server pages: https://histor.modelmarket.dev &middot; code: https://github.com/alexar76/histor</p>\n<p>License and rights</p>\n<p>The compilation, digests, labels, scans and verdicts are CC-BY-4.0: cite \"HISTOR,<br>https://histor.modelmarket.dev, snapshot 2026-10-20\". Tool names, descriptions and schemas are reproduced as each server<br>published them; their rights stay with their authors. They are included so the definitions can be<br>studied and checked. A server operator who wants out: open an issue on https://github.com/alexar76/histor with the<br>endpoint or host. Opted-out servers are left out of every later snapshot.</p>",
      "access_right": "open",
